<title>BRAZIL: Brazil May sugar exports ex-CS ports up on 1996.</title>
<headline>Brazil May sugar exports ex-CS ports up on 1996.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil sugar shipments out of key ports in the center-south region reached 118,166 tonnes in May against 108,097 tonnes in the same month last year, according to port authority statistics.</p>
<p>The bulk of the sugar was shipped out of the port of Paranagua which handled exports of 90,987 tonnes of sugar last month, dramatically higher than the 11,595 tonnes exported in May 1996, the port authority said.</p>
<p>The higher shipments are due to deliveries of 260,000 long tons of Paranagua raws against the New York May contract which should be completed by the middle of July.</p>
<p>A breakdown of shipments in tonnes as provided by individual port authorities follows.</p>
